# Your settings for Kamerplanter. A value here wins over the defaults in
# /usr/share/kamerplanter/kamerplanter.env, over the settings provisioned
# through cloud-init in /var/lib/kamerplanter/provisioning/ (kamerplanter: ->
# settings:, and a provisioning.env from write_files), and over the secrets
# generated in /etc/kamerplanter/secrets.env. This file survives updates and
# rollbacks; provisioning data never writes it.
# With a data disk, /etc/kamerplanter is on that disk: this file and the
# secrets live there, and a copy of this file starts it when it is set up.
#
# One KEY=VALUE per line, taken literally (no quotes are removed).
# Apply a change with:  systemctl restart kamerplanter.target
#
# Three values must not change once Kamerplanter has stored data; the
# appliance refuses to start if they do:
#   ERASURE_TOMBSTONE_SALT  keys the records of deleted accounts, never change
#   FERNET_KEY              encrypts stored credentials
#   ARANGODB_PASSWORD       the database keeps its first password; change it
#                           in the database first
# Back up /etc/kamerplanter/secrets.env together with your data; with a data
# disk, both are on that disk.
#
# Examples:
# CORS_ORIGINS=["https://kamerplanter.example.org"]
# FRONTEND_URL=https://kamerplanter.example.org
# REGISTRATION_MODE=invite_only
#
# A separate local data disk, formatted when blank (see the comments in
# /usr/share/kamerplanter/kamerplanter.env; ls -l /dev/disk/by-id/). Named
# here only while no data disk is set up; else use:
# /usr/libexec/kamerplanter/disks name data|backup PATH
# DATA_DISK=/dev/disk/by-id/usb-Example_Disk_0123456789-0:0
